Whisper: the Linux package carries install.sh

What: lists install.sh (browser/components/whisper/linux/) in the package, next to the
whisper program.
Why: the Linux tarball installs itself for the current user with it, without root: the
folder goes to ~/.local/share/whisper, where Whisper updates itself, with a menu entry,
icons and a whisper command; it also uninstalls, keeping the profile unless asked.
The package manifest lists every file that goes into a package, so a new one must be
named here.
---
diff --git a/browser/installer/package-manifest.in b/browser/installer/package-manifest.in
index 8d0a8e2aaa..14e2f11f2a 100644
--- a/browser/installer/package-manifest.in
+++ b/browser/installer/package-manifest.in
@@ -162,6 +162,10 @@
 @BINPATH@/@MOZ_APP_NAME@-bin
 #endif
 @BINPATH@/@MOZ_APP_NAME@
+#ifdef MOZ_WIDGET_GTK
+; Whisper: installs this copy for the current user (browser/components/whisper/linux/)
+@BINPATH@/install.sh
+#endif
 #endif
 @RESPATH@/application.ini
 #ifdef MOZ_UPDATER
